Assumptions and decisions
Public registration always creates a regular `user`; clients cannot grant themselves the `admin` role.
Regular users can create, list, view, edit, and delete their own tasks, but only administrators can update task status.
Administrators can access tasks across users and assign tasks when creating them.
The local seeder is for development/assessment use only.
Live AI functionality requires the developer's own Gemini API key; no key is included in the submission.